id: pm-graph-r58m
title: Investigate isolated package installation timeout with runtime dependencies
description: "The packaged-host regression setup repeatedly exceeded its 180-second timeout during pm package install, including offline mode. Determine whether dependency installation, archive staging or runtime verification is responsible; retain synthetic fixtures and report the exact cause without weakening read-output tests."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-13T13:36:32.154Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T18:35:42.677Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-13T18:51:46.257Z",codex-agent,The adoption release gates now pass their existing packed-extension installer tests under both npm and Bun launchers. The output-contract regression isolates its purpose by extracting the actual archive and reusing the pinned dependency graph. The earlier 180-second setup timeout has not been independently explained; retain this separate investigation.
  "2026-10-13T22:23:11.477Z",claude-hub,"Reopened: this item was linked in the merged PR body as an open follow-up or risk, not as delivered work. The automated close-out closed it in error; it remains open."
  "2026-10-16T06:41:53.166Z",codex-agent,"Current-main reproduction with the pinned PM CLI 2026.10.13 and an actual npm pack archive, clean HOME, shared registry cache and npm offline mode: pack 2.00s, init 1.96s, pm package install --project 29.77s, all exit 0. Installer reports activation ok, 15 commands, module_graph_verification=fresh_in_topology_snapshot and zero blocking health failures. A separate traced run also succeeds; tracing follows a detached flush helper and its elapsed wall time is not a reliable installer-only timing. The historical 180-second timeout is not reproduced and its original cause remains unproven; keep this investigation open rather than changing package behavior without a failing case."
  "2026-10-23T15:21:41.884Z",codex-agent,"STALE-CLAIM: audited main 13c51065d436e643cab250137dc6b43be4fa645b; no open PR or recently pushed live branch references this record. Inspected: test/export-and-contract.test.ts, test/read-output-host.test.ts. Remaining: The historical 180-second runtime-dependency install timeout no longer reproduces in the retained current-main probe; its original cause is still unproven. Keep root-cause investigation open without a speculative code change. Release historical contention and retain real work as open; no delivery/cancellation is claimed."
  "2026-10-27T17:21:34.388Z",codex-agent,"Additional public packed-host evidence from PR 175: a global shared npx cache lost package metadata during concurrent fleet activity, so validation now uses owned per-run npm/Bun caches. With a cold isolated cache, a public npm global install exceeded the old four-minute test-process deadline. The acceptance harness retains every assertion, permits ten minutes only for install/add operations, and disables install-time audit/funding chatter; the independent production audit release gate remains unchanged. Runtime CLI commands keep their original bounded timeout. Recovery functional checks already passed on npm and Bun global hosts before the cache failure; full rerun is tracked by pm-graph-event-sparse."
  "2026-10-27T18:00:55.126Z",codex-agent,"The final event-projection archive now passes actual npm-global and Bun-global consumers on the repository-pinned SDK: sixteen native Neo4j foreign-data refusals and eight post-action recoveries total. The isolated-cache run continues through ephemeral and project-local hosts. Future acceptance runs also use a private Node compile cache so repeated SDK host launches avoid unnecessary cold compilation on the shared host. Installation/add timeout remains bounded at ten minutes, runtime CLI timeout remains four minutes, and the independent production audit remains a release gate."
  "2026-10-27T18:35:42.661Z",codex-agent,"All six actual isolated-cache installation hosts now pass on pinned SDK 2026.10.23: npm/Bun global, npx/bunx and npm/Bun local. One verified 52-file archive supports 48 native ownership refusals and 24 crash recoveries across formats/modes. Shared-cache ENOENT is avoided by per-run private caches; ten-minute installation timeout and four-minute runtime timeout remain bounded. No production gate or threshold was weakened."
